# Modal chrome vs content padding

Fullscreen and split modals (MediaModal, InteractiveModal, in-demo views like Photo Critique) often need **header/footer inset** without shrinking the **middle** media or demo stage.

## Source of truth

- [`src/lib/modalLayout.ts`](src/lib/modalLayout.ts)
  - `MODAL_VIEWPORT_INNER` — **max-width + flex column only**. Never put `px-*` / site gutters here.
  - `MODAL_TOPBAR_PAD_X` — same as SiteNav (`px-3 sm:px-5 md:px-10`) on the **close/date top bar** so the X lines up with the menu toggle when the modal closes. Mobile stays `px-3` (unchanged vs before).
- `MODAL_CHROME_PAD_X` — `px-3` for other chrome (tabs, actions, context copy, seek/thumbs/CTA). Not site-nav gutters.
- Media modal video **seek / thumb strip / visit CTA** share chrome pad via `ChromelessYouTubePlayer` (seek row) and MediaModal wrappers — hero uses a separate seek UI and must not inherit this.

## Do

- Put horizontal padding on **chrome rows only**: close / date header, tab bars, overlay toggles, bottom action buttons.
- Keep the **middle scroll / preview / embed / demo stage** flush to the content column (micro-insets like `pl-[6px]` only when explicitly requested).
- Left **text context** columns may use `MODAL_CHROME_PAD_X` so copy clears the edge on mobile; the **right media/demo** column stays flush.

## Do not

- Wrap the entire modal body (header + middle + footer) in one `px-*` / `p-*` / `sm:px-5 md:px-10` container.
- Put SiteNav gutters (`px-3 sm:px-5 md:px-10`) on `MODAL_VIEWPORT_INNER` — that pads the middle and fights full-bleed demos.
- “Fix” demo edge spacing by padding the shared viewport wrapper.

